## Architecture Issues

### [ARCH-001] Clean Architecture Violation - Auth Depends on EF

**File:** `MrWhoOidc.Auth/MrWhoOidc.Auth.csproj`
**Severity:** MAJOR

**Issue:**
The `MrWhoOidc.Auth` project directly references Entity Framework Core packages (`Microsoft.EntityFrameworkCore`, `Npgsql.EntityFrameworkCore.PostgreSQL`, etc.). This violates Clean Architecture principles where the domain/core layer should not depend on infrastructure concerns.

**Evidence:**
xml
<ItemGroup>
  <PackageReference Include="Microsoft.EntityFrameworkCore" Version="10.0.1" />
  <PackageReference Include="Microsoft.EntityFrameworkCore.Relational" Version="10.0.1" />
  <PackageReference Include="Npgsql.EntityFrameworkCore.PostgreSQL" Version="10.0.0" />
  <PackageReference Include="Microsoft.EntityFrameworkCore.InMemory" Version="10.0.1" />
  <PackageReference Include="Microsoft.EntityFrameworkCore.Design" Version="10.0.1">
    <PrivateAssets>all</PrivateAssets>
    <IncludeAssets>runtime; build; native; contentfiles; analyzers; buildtransitive</IncludeAssets>
  </PackageReference>
</ItemGroup>


**Remediation:**
Create a separate `MrWhoOidc.Auth.Infrastructure` project and move EF Core dependencies there:

1. **Create new project:** `MrWhoOidc.Auth.Infrastructure`
2. **Move EF packages:** Move all EF Core package references to the Infrastructure project
3. **Define interfaces in Auth:** Keep domain entities and repository interfaces in `MrWhoOidc.Auth`
4. **Implement in Infrastructure:** Implement `AuthDbContext` and repository classes in `MrWhoOidc.Auth.Infrastructure`

Example structure:

MrWhoOidc.Auth/                    # Domain layer (no EF deps)
  ├── Entities/
  ├── Interfaces/
  │   └── IAuthDbContext.cs
  └── Services/

MrWhoOidc.Auth.Infrastructure/    # Infrastructure layer (EF deps)
  ├── Persistence/
  │   └── AuthDbContext.cs
  └── Repositories/


Interface definition in Auth:
csharp
// MrWhoOidc.Auth/Interfaces/IAuthDbContext.cs
public interface IAuthDbContext
{
    DbSet<User> Users { get; }
    DbSet<Client> Clients { get; }
    Task<int> SaveChangesAsync(CancellationToken cancellationToken = default);
}


Implementation in Infrastructure:
csharp
// MrWhoOidc.Auth.Infrastructure/Persistence/AuthDbContext.cs
public class AuthDbContext : DbContext, IAuthDbContext
{
    // EF-specific implementation
}


### [SRP-001] AuthDbContext Violates Single Responsibility Principle

**File:** `MrWhoOidc.Auth/Persistence/AuthDbContext.cs`
**Lines:** 1-2137
**Severity:** MAJOR

**Issue:**
The `AuthDbContext` class is 2,137 lines long and handles multiple responsibilities:
- Database configuration (40+ DbSets)
- GUID collision resolution
- Email normalization
- Entity relationship configuration

This violates the Single Responsibility Principle and makes the class difficult to maintain, test, and understand.

**Evidence:**
csharp
public class AuthDbContext : DbContext, IDataProtectionKeyContext
{
    // 40+ DbSet properties
    public DbSet<Tenant> Tenants => Set<Tenant>();
    public DbSet<UserAccount> UserAccounts => Set<UserAccount>();
    // ... 38 more DbSets

    // GUID collision logic
    private async Task EnsureUserPrimaryKeysAvailableAsync(CancellationToken cancellationToken)
    {
        // 50+ lines of collision resolution logic
    }

    // Email normalization logic
    void NormalizeEmailFields()
    {
        // 40+ lines of email normalization
    }

    // Entity configuration
    protected override void OnModelCreating(ModelBuilder modelBuilder)
    {
        // 1800+ lines of entity configuration
    }
}


**Remediation:**
Extract responsibilities into separate classes:

1. **Create IEntityTypeConfiguration classes** for each entity:
csharp
// MrWhoOidc.Auth/Persistence/Configurations/UserConfiguration.cs
public class UserConfiguration : IEntityTypeConfiguration<User>
{
    public void Configure(EntityTypeBuilder<User> builder)
    {
        builder.HasKey(x => x.Id);
        builder.Property(x => x.Username).IsRequired().HasMaxLength(200);
        builder.HasIndex(x => new { x.TenantId, x.Username }).IsUnique();
        // ... rest of User configuration
    }
}


2. **Create a GUID collision service**:
csharp
// MrWhoOidc.Auth/Services/GuidCollisionResolver.cs
public interface IGuidCollisionResolver
{
    Task EnsureUniqueIdsAsync(IEnumerable<User> users, CancellationToken cancellationToken);
}

public class GuidCollisionResolver : IGuidCollisionResolver
{
    private readonly AuthDbContext _context;
    private readonly ILogger<GuidCollisionResolver> _logger;

    public GuidCollisionResolver(AuthDbContext context, ILogger<GuidCollisionResolver> logger)
    {
        _context = context;
        _logger = logger;
    }

    public async Task EnsureUniqueIdsAsync(IEnumerable<User> users, CancellationToken cancellationToken)
    {
        // Move GUID collision logic here
    }
}


3. **Create an email normalizer service**:
csharp
// MrWhoOidc.Auth/Services/EmailNormalizationService.cs
public interface IEmailNormalizationService
{
    void NormalizeEmailFields(ChangeTracker changeTracker);
}

public class EmailNormalizationService : IEmailNormalizationService
{
    public void NormalizeEmailFields(ChangeTracker changeTracker)
    {
        // Move email normalization logic here
    }
}


4. **Simplified AuthDbContext**:
csharp
public class AuthDbContext : DbContext, IDataProtectionKeyContext
{
    private readonly IGuidCollisionResolver _guidResolver;
    private readonly IEmailNormalizationService _emailNormalizer;

    public AuthDbContext(
        DbContextOptions<AuthDbContext> options,
        IGuidCollisionResolver guidResolver,
        IEmailNormalizationService emailNormalizer)
        : base(options)
    {
        _guidResolver = guidResolver;
        _emailNormalizer = emailNormalizer;
    }

    // DbSet properties only
    public DbSet<User> Users => Set<User>();
    // ... other DbSets

    public override async Task<int> SaveChangesAsync(CancellationToken cancellationToken = default)
    {
        var pendingUsers = ChangeTracker.Entries<User>()
            .Where(e => e.State == EntityState.Added)
            .Select(e => e.Entity)
            .ToList();

        await _guidResolver.EnsureUniqueIdsAsync(pendingUsers, cancellationToken);
        _emailNormalizer.NormalizeEmailFields(ChangeTracker);

        return await base.SaveChangesAsync(cancellationToken);
    }

    protected override void OnModelCreating(ModelBuilder modelBuilder)
    {
        base.OnModelCreating(modelBuilder);

        // Apply all configurations
        modelBuilder.ApplyConfigurationsFromAssembly(typeof(AuthDbContext).Assembly);
        ConfigureLicenseEntities(modelBuilder);
    }
}


